      "exercise": "979",
      "source_number": "979",
      "group": "第40小节",
      "group_id": "g9",
      "pages": ["p0295#4"],
      "figure_refs": [],
      "source_text": "979. 解下列方程：а) $(x-10)\\sqrt{x-4}=0$； б) $(x+4)\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{x-2}}=0$；в) $(x-1)\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{x-3}}=0$； г) $(x+2)\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{x+2}}=0$；д) $\\frac{x-6}{2x-4}\\sqrt{x-2}=0$； е) $\\frac{6-2x}{9-x}\\sqrt{x-9}=0$。",
      "modern_text": "979. 解下列方程：\na) $(x-10)\\sqrt{x-4}=0$；\nb) $(x+4)\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{x-2}}=0$；\nc) $(x-1)\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{x-3}}=0$；\nd) $(x+2)\\sqrt{\\frac{x-5}{x+2}}=0$；\ne) $\\frac{x-6}{2x-4}\\sqrt{x-2}=0$；\nf) $\\frac{6-2x}{9-x}\\sqrt{x-9}=0$。",
      "hashes": {
        "raw_record_sha256": "005312e68aaf21be274ed8262a1e8ca86c8536816b5e777bde033999c36c3e9b",
        "raw_text_sha256": "2ac32d62bd814e84cba5d816f7093dffd9021c3c1536ccdc392fec676c958e90",
        "modern_record_sha256": "990e5d3e2fcd97bc4a2cdfac292caed2a643bf6a612195113651fad8141e5d35",
        "modern_text_sha256": "d76b60af4d80b46f3261baa581bde1a7252d9c82e9337d39dfc6d7a81080244f"
      },
      "task": "Solve each equation on its original real domain.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a", "source_label": "а",
          "answer": "x\\in\\{4,10\\}",
          "domain": "x\\in[4,\\infty); no denominator.",
          "derivation": "x-4>=0. A product vanishes if x-10=0 or its principal root sqrt(x-4)=0, giving x=10 or x=4. Both are in the original domain and make the original product zero."
        },
        {
          "label": "b", "source_label": "б",
          "answer": "x\\in\\{-4,0\\}",
          "domain": "x/(x-2)>=0 and x!=2, hence x\\in(-\\infty,0]\\cup(2,\\infty).",
          "derivation": "The factor x+4 vanishes at -4; the radicand vanishes at 0. Both are allowed: at -4 the radicand is 2/3 and at 0 it is 0; neither denominator is zero."
        },
        {
          "label": "c", "source_label": "в",
          "answer": "x=0",
          "domain": "x/(x-3)>=0 and x!=3, hence x\\in(-\\infty,0]\\cup(3,\\infty).",
          "derivation": "The candidates are x=1 from x-1=0 and x=0 from the principal root. Reject x=1 because the radicand is -1/2; x=0 is defined and solves the original equation."
        },
        {
          "label": "d", "source_label": "г",
          "answer": "x=5",
          "domain": "(x-5)/(x+2)>=0 and x!=-2, hence x\\in(-\\infty,-2)\\cup[5,\\infty).",
          "derivation": "The apparent factor-zero candidate x=-2 is excluded by the original radicand denominator. The root vanishes at x=5, whose denominator is 7, so x=5 is the only solution."
        },
        {
          "label": "e", "source_label": "д",
          "answer": "x=6",
          "domain": "x-2>=0 and 2x-4!=0, hence x\\in(2,\\infty).",
          "derivation": "A defined quotient times the root vanishes only at x=6 from the numerator or x=2 from the root. Reject x=2 because 2x-4=0. At x=6 the denominator is 8 and the quotient is zero."
        },
        {
          "label": "f", "source_label": "е",
          "answer": "\\varnothing",
          "domain": "x-9>=0 and 9-x!=0, hence x\\in(9,\\infty).",
          "derivation": "The numerator vanishes at x=3, outside the root domain. The root vanishes at x=9, where the original denominator is zero. For every x>9 the quotient and root are nonzero, so there is no real solution."
        }
      ],
      "uncertainties": []
    },
    {
      "exercise": "980",
      "source_number": "980",
      "group": "第41小节",
      "group_id": "g10",
